# LLM Gateway — Cursor Rules

## Language and framework

- TypeScript strict mode. No `any` type, ever. Use `unknown` and narrow it.
- NestJS with module/service/repository/controller separation.
- Prisma for all DB access. Raw `$queryRaw` only for complex aggregations.
- BullMQ for async post-response work. Never do DB writes on the hot path.

## Code style

- No `console.log` anywhere in `src/`. Use `new Logger(ClassName.name)`.
- No comments explaining what code does. Only comment WHY when it's non-obvious.
- No multi-line docstrings. One short line max if a comment is needed at all.
- No `any` in test files. Use proper jest mocked types.
- Prefer editing existing files over creating new ones.
- No features, abstractions, or error handling beyond what the task requires.

## Architecture patterns (read before touching these areas)

- Adapters (`src/modules/providers/adapters/`) follow a plugin pattern. No constructor
  dependencies. Instantiated with `new()` in `onModuleInit`. See ADR-001.

- BullMQ jobs run after `res.end()`, never before. `StreamService.proxy()` calls
  `onComplete()` after the last SSE chunk. See ADR-002.

- Rate limiting uses a Lua script in `sliding-window.lua`. The order is:
  `estimateTokens → checkRpm → budget GET → checkTpm`. Do not reorder. See ADR-003.

- Cache interceptor uses `of(null)` not `EMPTY` on cache hits. `EMPTY` causes EmptyError.
  Cache key: SHA-256(tenantId+provider+model+messages+params). See ADR-004.

- `AdminGuard` and `AuthGuard` are completely separate. Never put `AdminGuard` on tenant
  endpoints or `AuthGuard` on management endpoints. See ADR-005.

## Security rules (never violate)

- `x-user-id` header / `userLabel` field must be an opaque token. Never store emails,
  names, or real user identifiers. Callers pseudonymize before sending.
- Message content limits: 100 messages max, 1M characters per message. Do not raise.
- `AdminGuard` on all management endpoints (providers, tenants, key creation).
- Raw provider API keys never stored — encrypt with AES-256-GCM via `encryption.util.ts`.
- Every Redis key must be prefixed with `tenant:{id}:`.
- Every DB query must include `tenantId` scoping (BaseRepository enforces this).

## Database rules

- Prisma UUID fields: `String @db.Uuid`, not `UUID`.
- FK scalar fields declared before their `@relation` lines.
- Every new table (except `tenants`) needs `tenantId String @db.Uuid`.
- PII-sensitive columns must have a comment in `schema.prisma`.
- Aggregation queries use `usage_daily`, not raw `requests` table (O(rows) at scale).
- `$queryRaw` results: always call `Number(row.field)` on DECIMAL columns — Prisma returns
  Decimal objects that JSON.stringify as `{ "d": [...] }` not plain numbers.
- `$queryRaw` WHERE clauses: use `Prisma.sql` tagged templates, never string concatenation.

## Repository exceptions (documented, intentional)

- `TenantsRepository` does NOT extend `BaseRepository` — Tenant has no `tenantId` FK.
- `RouterRepository` does NOT extend `BaseRepository` — needs NULL-aware tenant query.
- Do not refactor either of these.

## Testing

- Mock SDK packages at module level: `jest.mock('openai')` not `jest.spyOn(prototype)`.
- `ioredis-mock` for Redis tests — it executes Lua natively.
- Integration tests: `const runTest = apiKey ? it : it.skip` (no real keys in CI).
- No test should hit a real external API unless explicitly flagged as integration.

## Commit format

`type(scope): description` — types: feat | fix | docs | refactor | test | chore | perf

## Key reference files

- Architecture: `.claude/docs/architecture.md`
- ADRs: `docs/decisions/ADR-001` through `ADR-005`
- Per-module context: `src/modules/<name>/CLAUDE.md`
- Task history: `.claude/docs/tasks.md`
- Slash commands: `.claude/commands/`
